  "material_note": "horse_drawn_01 is a 256-square atlas and the sheet most of this batch is built from: a cart wheel, sawn planks, crates and a few dark iron fittings, all in one square. One sheet is one material on the tiled path and timber is what most of it is, so the iron is left as the painting it already is.",
  "cutout": [
    "grass_01"
  ],
  "cutout_from": "Real alpha in grass_01.OZT, as on Straw01.",
  "cutout_soften": {
    "grass_01": [
      2.5,
      0.8
    ]
  },
  "cutout_soften_from": "The straw's comb of tips is finer than a pixel from the game's camera and crawled as it moved; blurred across the strands so they merge. Ours, not MU's. See pipeline/soften_alpha.py.",
  "uv_heal": true,
  "uv_heal_from": "MU maps one side of each bundle onto a line of its sheet (u 0.972 to 1.0), so that side is one smeared column with the comb's holes dragged across it, which shimmered as the hero walked past. u laid across those faces at the mesh's own density; v kept. Ours, not MU's. See clean_lowpoly.heal_collapsed.",
  "sheet_pad": {
    "horse_drawn_01": "edge"
  },
  "sheet_pad_from": "An atlas rather than a tile - separate objects drawn side by side in one square - so its border replicates instead of wrapping. Wrapped, the wheel's iron rim is fed into the planks as context and the model invents a rim along a bare board.",
  "sheet_scale": {
    "grass_01": 1.0
  },
  "sheet_roughness": {
    "horse_drawn_01": 0.95
  },
  "sheet_roughness_from": "The user's, 2026-10-11, at the warehouse, 148,144: 'i dont like it that its so glossy'. Timber's 0.82 still laid a sheen along the cart's planks in the moon and the lamps; 0.95, dry weathered wood, leaves MU's painted grain to carry it. On every object that wears this sheet, so the carts match.",
